# LifeFlow Location Platform (English backup)

LifeFlow now has a local factual location foundation built from the existing OSM,
OSRM and accommodation data. It includes:

- PostgreSQL 16 with PostGIS 3.5 in an isolated Docker volume
- Canonical places with source traceability
- Housing property, unit, listing and offer schemas
- A typed Housing Query service with hard PostGIS filters
- A Platform API on `127.0.0.1:4100`
- Six read-only MCP tools over `stdio`
- The existing MapLibre app on `127.0.0.1:5173`
- Three existing OSRM services for HCM, Hanoi and Da Nang
- The original GeoJSON as a frontend fallback

The current source contains 13,120 POI features, published as 13,118 canonical
places plus two duplicate source IDs. No housing listing source has been supplied,
so production housing search correctly returns an empty result instead of invented
records.

## Daily Start

1. Start Docker Desktop and wait until Docker Engine is running.
2. Open PowerShell.
3. Run:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow\Start-LifeFlow.ps1"
```

4. Open:

```text
Map: http://127.0.0.1:5173/
API health: http://127.0.0.1:4100/health
```

The start script safely:

1. Starts `lifeflow-postgis` on port `5433`.
2. Starts `osrm-hcm`, `osrm-hanoi` and `osrm-danang`.
3. Builds the backend and applies checksum-protected migrations.
4. Starts the Platform API.
5. Starts the MapLibre frontend.

It does not reimport data, delete data or recreate Docker volumes.

## Daily Stop

Press `Ctrl+C` in the PowerShell window that is running the frontend, then run:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow\Stop-LifeFlow.ps1"
```

This stops the LifeFlow API, the three OSRM containers and the LifeFlow PostGIS
container. It does not remove containers, volumes, databases, images or source
files.

## Architecture

```text
MapLibre frontend
  |-- visible-city POI requests --> Platform API --> PostGIS
  |-- fallback ------------------> accommodations.geojson
  `-- interactive route --------> city OSRM

LifeFlow Agent
  `-- MCP stdio server
        |-- search_housing / get_housing --> Housing Query --> PostGIS
        |-- search_places / get_place ----> Place Query ---> PostGIS
        |-- find_nearby_places -----------> PostGIS
        `-- calculate_route -------------> OSRM
```

The factual subsystem never ranks, scores or recommends housing. A separately
owned recommendation module may consume these contracts and results later.

## Platform API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/health` | PostgreSQL/PostGIS health |
| `POST` | `/v1/places/search` | Text/category/spatial place search |
| `GET` | `/v1/places/:placeId` | Canonical place details |
| `POST` | `/v1/places/nearby` | Indexed nearby-place lookup |
| `POST` | `/v1/housing/search` | Factual housing hard filters |
| `GET` | `/v1/housing/:listingId` | Housing listing details |
| `POST` | `/v1/routes` | OSRM distance, duration and geometry |

The API is bound to loopback for local development.

## MCP Server

Build and run the local MCP server:

```powershell
Set-Location "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow"
npm run build
npm run dev:mcp
```

For an MCP client, use:

```json
{
  "command": "node",
  "args": [
    "D:\\Bản đồ VN\\LifeFlow\\mcp-server\\dist\\server.js"
  ],
  "env": {
    "LIFEFLOW_ENV_FILE": "D:\\Bản đồ VN\\LifeFlow\\.env"
  }
}
```

Published tools:

```text
search_housing
get_housing
search_places
get_place
find_nearby_places
calculate_route
```

There is deliberately no `recommend_housing` tool.

## Import Updated POI Data

The importer reads the source file configured by `POI_SOURCE_PATH`. It preserves
source payloads, records checksums and import counts, and does not overwrite
`lifeflow_verified` records.

```powershell
Set-Location "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow"
npm run db:up
npm run db:migrate
npm run db:import:places
```

Keep versioned source files. Do not overwrite a working OSM/PBF file in place.
OSM refreshes and custom LifeFlow records are source-aware, so custom records are
not removed by an OSM import.

## Adding Housing Data

Housing data must be mapped into:

```text
catalog.places
  -> housing.properties
  -> housing.units
  -> housing.listings
  -> housing.offers
```

Do not insert demo records into the production database. Add a source-specific
ingestion adapter that records provenance in `integration.source_records`.
Once real listings are imported, the existing API and MCP search filters become
available without changing their contracts.

## Validation

```powershell
Set-Location "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow"
npm run build
npm test

Set-Location "D:\Bản đồ VN\LifeFlow\map-app"
npm run lint
npm run build
npm run test:e2e
```

The current implementation result is recorded in
`docs/HOUSING-QUERY-IMPLEMENTATION.md`.
